config-connector-extensions patch 0027: mockgcp's routers.get leaves out MD5 key values.

For compute.gcp.hfl.dev ComputeRouter. Written here: a router read with
routers.get carries each of its md5AuthenticationKeys by name only, without
the key, as the real API does (Terraform's google_compute_router_peer
reads it so: "key value is not returned as it is a sensitive field"). The
stored router keeps the key. Upstream candidate: yes.

diff --git a/mockgcp/mockcompute/routersv1.go b/mockgcp/mockcompute/routersv1.go
index 7c11d712..758004fa 100644
--- a/mockgcp/mockcompute/routersv1.go
+++ b/mockgcp/mockcompute/routersv1.go
@@ -55,6 +55,12 @@ func (s *RoutersV1) Get(ctx context.Context, req *pb.GetRouterRequest) (*pb.Rout
 		obj.EncryptedInterconnectRouter = nil
 	}
 
+	// The API keeps an MD5 authentication key's value but never returns it:
+	// a read has each key's name only.
+	for _, key := range obj.Md5AuthenticationKeys {
+		key.Key = nil
+	}
+
 	return obj, nil
 }
 
